## When the user asks you to improve something (not a bug, not a whole feature)

New keyboard shortcut, another supported file format, a faster query, splitting a 400-line module. Nothing is broken, and there is no PRD to write.

1. **Plan.** Precedent (how does this codebase already do the nearest thing?), scope, and an explicit **`Done when:`** list — the acceptance criteria for a change that has none on file.
2. **Apply**, with a test per `Done when:` condition.
3. **Review**, scoped: bug hunt and test quality always; then exactly one of security / fidelity / edge probe, picked by what the diff touches. The requirements pass does not run — there are no persisted acceptance criteria — so the test-quality pass carries the `Done when:` check and reports per-condition pass/fail. Any uncovered condition is a blocker.
4. **Both changelogs**, under `### Improved` — but only if a user can see the change. Pure refactors and perf work stay in the engineering log.

On `main`/`master`, ask before starting; branch by default.

---

## When the user asks you to fix a bug

1. **Diagnose root cause.** Don't patch the symptom. Trace it back to where the contract was broken.
2. **Write a failing test** that reproduces the bug. Run it — confirm it fails.
3. **Surgical fix.** One bug, one fix. No tangential cleanup in the same change.
4. **Run a focused bug-hunt review of the fix** — does it resolve the root cause, does it introduce new risk, would the test actually catch the regression, what is adjacent enough to need re-testing. This is one pass, not the full six.
5. **Append to engineering changelog.** Append to product changelog only if users would have seen the bug.
6. **Record what was learned** — a binding decision goes to `./docs/DECISIONS.md`, anything needed before touching this code again goes to `./docs/MEMORY.md`.

On `main`/`master`, ask before starting; a bug fix is usually fine to land there, but it is the user's call.

---

## Test execution rules

Never use watch mode. Always run tests to completion in a single shot.

- **Vitest:** `vitest run` or `npx vitest run` — never bare `vitest`
- **Jest:** `jest` (default is non-watch) — never `--watch` / `--watchAll`
- **Pytest:** `pytest` — never `pytest-watch` / `ptw`
- **Go:** `go test ./...`
- **Other:** pass the explicit one-shot / non-watch flag

This applies to every test invocation, including "quick checks."

---

## Human checkpoints

Stop and wait for the user before continuing past any of these points:

- Approach selection (after presenting 3 options)
- PRD approval (after resolving all `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` items)
- Constitution violations (must be resolved or explicitly waived)
- Implementation plan (before writing any code)
- Design approval (mobile-first, then desktop, separately)

**Under `--auto` the plan and PRD gates are skipped** — they are approval ceremony, and auto mode exists to skip ceremony. Three exceptions re-arm them regardless: a plan that adds a dependency or changes a public interface, an unresolved pre-review finding on a Contract claim, and anything on the always-pause list under "Auto Mode" below. Constitution violations and destructive operations are never skipped.

---

## What "done" means for a story

All of the following must be true before marking a story complete:

- All acceptance criteria met (binary check)
- Tests pass in non-watch mode
- No constitution violations
- Review across 7 areas produced no blockers
- Decisions and project memory recorded
- Both changelogs updated
- Conventional commit created (**not** pushed — pushing is always the user's call)
- (If UI) fidelity check passes

If any of these fail, the story is not done.

---

## Focus pointer (`.agentic/focus.md`)

`.agentic/focus.md` is a per-worktree pointer to the current task. Section `# CURRENT` holds the active task (`title:`, `feature:`, `since:`, `set_by:`, `note:`). Section `# NEXT` is an ordered list of queued items. The file lives in `.agentic/` which is gitignored — each worktree has its own state, no cross-worktree stomping.

Operations on it — the user may name them as slash commands if they come from Claude Code, but they are plain file edits:

- **set focus** — overwrite CURRENT with the named task.
- **finish focus** — clear CURRENT and, if NEXT is non-empty, ask which of three to do: promote item #1 to CURRENT, clear only, or move it to the backlog. Ask it as a choice, not as a typed `y`/`n`/`b` reply.
- **clear focus** — wipe both sections.
- **queue** — append to NEXT; drop item N to remove one.

Write CURRENT at the start of any long-running operation, using a story-id-match heuristic that prevents flicker when one operation is nested in another: if the new task references the same story or feature as the existing CURRENT, update only `note:` and `set_by:` and leave `title:`, `since:` and `# PLAN` alone. Multi-phase work also writes one `# PLAN` line per phase and ticks them off as phases close — PLAN is the progress record, and it survives a context compaction.

Any tool can surface the current task by reading the `title:` field of `# CURRENT` in `.agentic/focus.md`. (Claude Code wires this into its statusline during project setup; nothing else in this workflow depends on that.)

---

## Auto Mode (`--auto`)

Long-running operations accept a `--auto` flag: feature research, fix, improve, ship, ship-all, implement, design, doc. Under `--auto`, the agent skips ceremonial checkpoints and applies defaults from `./docs/CONSTITUTION.md` (especially a `## Default Decisions` section, if present). Every auto-decision is announced inline (`DECISION: <choice> — reason: <why> [auto]`) and appended to `.agentic/auto-log.md` (gitignored, alongside `.agentic/focus.md`).

The agent always pauses regardless of `--auto` for:
- Review blockers (high-severity bugs, requirements miss, constitution violation)
- Destructive operations (CI configs, secrets, force-push, DB migrations, mass deletes)
- Constitution conflicts
- Missing required project state (no test framework, no design tool, no feature directory)

End of command prints a one-line summary referring to the log file: `🤖 Auto mode: <D> decisions, <S> skips, <H> hard-pauses. See .agentic/auto-log.md`.
